#
# === PROVISIONAL under two-tick discipline (READ THIS) ===
#
# This shard is minted at `shards/mirror/index.mirror` as the readable
# name (tick 1). Its foundational home is `shards/fractal/index.mirror`
# under the `@fractal` family-root (tick 2). The collapse target is
# NAMED explicitly here so Reed's Landing 3/4/5 wire against the stable
# import path today; when Alex adjudicates roadmap-15 `#6` (the
# @fractal family-root shape), the file MOVES — not the actions, not
# the types, not the composition surface. The imports do a one-tick
# rename; the substrate-decl content is invariant under the collapse.
#
# Why @mirror/index and not @spectral/index: `shards/spectral.mirror`
# was shrunk to namespace-parent-only 2026-07-01 per Recognition #46
# second instance (Loki §5; Seam-ratified `17f0ee5`). @spectral is a
# runtime namespace for db/garden/portal/gen_prism — NOT the
# observation/measurement altitude. Placing `index` under @spectral
# would re-inflate the family root the substrate refused. @mirror is
# the correct provisional home because Recognition #43 (mirror IS
# content-addressed build system) grounds the DAG this shard measures.
#
# Why @fractal is the foundational home: Alex 2026-07-13 in-transcript
# ("With @fractal the compiler becomes basically a Mandelbrot set"),
# Mara `2c64060` (`docs/specs/fractal-family-root-mandelbrot-substrate.md`)
# and Mara `3ffa8ed` (`docs/math/2026-07-13-fractal-mandelbrot-substrate.md`)
# identify the substrate with the Mandelbrot set: `M∘` IS @magic's
# gauge-bounded interior (#80); `∂M` IS @io's Turing-unbounded boundary
# (#107); the three-state `verdict` closes at three because M's topology
# closes at three. The Fiedler reading this shard names is one carrier
# of @fractal-coherence at the file-tree altitude. Roadmap-15 `#6`
# (`docs/roadmap/15-fractal-membrane-Asher-tripartition.md`) parks the
# family-root mint on Alex adjudication; the collapse target is
# `shards/fractal/index.mirror` under `prism @fractal { … }`.
#
# === What @mirror/index IS ===
#
# @mirror/index IS the substrate's own measurement of its
# @fractal-coherence at the file-tree altitude. Given a peer_home
# directory, it walks the file-tree, classifies files by grammar kind
# (markdown / code / config / .mirror / asset / gestalt-native /
# unknown), assembles a directory-node concept graph with
# Contains / SimilarContent / CrossRef edges, and returns the
# eigenvalue profile of the graph's sheaf-Laplacian — with the Fiedler
# value λ₀(Δ_F) as the load-bearing scalar.
#
# Per Taut `b52b008` empirical scout (docs/scouts/2026-07-13-taut-
# fiedler-as-lambda-zero-empirical-scout.md): the Fiedler 0.0612 value
# on this repo (1138 files, 165 nodes, 6676 edges) IS λ₀(Δ_F) — 6%
# residual H¹(F) obstruction empirically confirmed. The measurement is
# real; the shard IS the substrate-decl of its owner altitude.
#
# === Form/process partition (#55) grounds this altitude ===
#
# Per Recognition #55 (form/process partition; DAG is form, measurement
# is process; belong at the same altitude): the DAG (`@mirror/store`)
# and its measurement (this shard) are sibling species under @mirror
# provisionally, and under @fractal foundationally. The DAG carries the
# content; the measurement reads the content's coherence. Neither
# contains the other; both project the same five-operation algebra
# through their own typed surface.
#
# Per Recognition #43 (mirror IS content-addressed build system): the
# substrate ALREADY OWNS the content-addressed DAG (@mirror/store's
# six-op surface). This shard closes the last gap in Bazel-REAPI-floor
# decomposition — reads its own DAG's algebraic connectivity. Every
# build system that names the DAG must also name the DAG's coherence
# metric; mirror's coherence metric is λ₀(Δ_F), and this shard is where
# the substrate names it in-substrate.
#
# === Composition with existing substrate ===
#
# Consumes `@mirror/store` graph — the walked file-tree IS the CAS's
# splinter_graph (root, children) shape at the file-directory altitude
# per Recognition #43. This shard reads the store's shape at
# @io-crossing time; the store's canonical six-op surface (read /
# write / exists / diff / walk / verify per `shards/mirror/store.mirror`)
# is the substrate the walk projects through.
#
# Composes `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.lambda_zero` — the
# LAPACK `dsyev` primitive T8-landed at `shards/epistemologic/math/
# sheaf_laplacian.mirror` per Bodnar et al. 2022 §2's exact δ*δ
# construction. THIS IS THE LOAD-BEARING SUBSTRATE-PULL WIN per Taut
# §6: mirror's numerical floor already claims the altitude; the
# migration routes the file-directory concept-graph Laplacian THROUGH
# `sheaf_laplacian::sheaf_laplacian` + `lambda_zero`, NOT through
# spectral's hand-rolled Jacobi. Landing 3 discharges this composition
# in Rust.
#
# Feeds `@kintsugi/consent.query_phi` verdict — the three-state floor
# (pass | partial(confidence) | failure(reason)) IS one branch of the
# consent surface the auto-apply boundary rides. Consent EMERGES from
# @fractal at auto-apply altitude per Mara `2c64060` §5; this shard's
